        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T23:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do you think we should investigate that?\n\nYes, that seems worth double-checking. Is it the same on Zephyr and EC?\n\nIf you want to check it separately from this CL, you can file a bug and add a `TODO(b/123)`.\n\nMy guess is that maybe the `memcpy` implementation is highly optimized (copying whole words, not single bytes) and maybe `memmove` is using a very basic implementation (e.g., individual bytes).",
      "parentUuid": "4c8bb822_fb20404c",
